  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Junaid Shafi Bhat vs Ut Of J&K And Others on 4 April, 2024 Author: Rahul Bharti Bench: Rahul Bharti High Court Of Jammu &Kashmir And Ladakh At Srinagar Reserved on: 28.03.2024 Pronounced on: 04.04.2024 Wp (Crl) No. 614/2022 Junaid Shafi Bhat ... Petitioner/Appellant(s) Through: Ms. Razia Amin, Advocate V/s Ut of J&K and others ... Respondent(s) Through: Mr. Faheem Nissar Shah, Ga Coram: Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Rahul Bharti, Judge Judgment 1. 3 -District Magistrate Anantnag",
    "facts": "2. The petitioner is 24 years old young man who has come to suffer loss of his personal liberty by preventive detention custody ordered against him by the respondent No.3 - District Magistrate Anantnag vide an Order No. 49/DMA/PSA/DET/2022 dated 29/06/2022 (hereinafter to be referred in short as \"the detention order\") passed under the J&K Public Safety Act, 1978 on the purported ground that the petitioner's alleged activities were reckoned to be prejudicial to \"the Security of the State\".",
    "arguments": "5. Drawing from the said dossier, the respondent no. 3-District Magistrate Anantnag came to set out the grounds of detention based upon which a subjective satisfaction was purportedly formed by the respondent No.3-District Magistrate Anantnag that the petitioner deserves deprivation of his personal liberty otherwise a guaranteed fundamental right of the petitioner. 6. The grounds of detention profiled the petitioner by reference to his brother Umais Shafi Bhat who got killed in an encounter with Security Forces at Takiya Maqsood Shah Bijbehara on 23/11/2018 as he was alleged to be affiliated with terrorist organisation \"HM\". The petitioner is alleged to have made close contact with the banned terrorist organisation HM with an aim and intention to provide logistic support in terms of food/shelter/car transportation to terrorist from one place to another in the outskirts of Bijbehara town and also carrying out the task of keeping a close vigil on the Security Forces. With this background the petitioner was reckoned to be a risk to be let free in the wake of annual Amarnath Yatra. The petitioner was alleged to be working on the direction of militants whose aim was to disrupt the peaceful atmosphere and to secede the UT of J&K from the rest of the Country."
  },
